  "thesis": "When cumulative signed BTC volume has a positive short-versus-long moving-average state, broad participation may confirm price demand strongly enough that a next-open long/cash policy preserves most upside while avoiding enough weak-flow downside to improve fee-adjusted path risk over full-capital buy-and-hold.",
  "economic_rationale": "OBV accumulates complete-day volume with the sign of the daily close return, so its moving-average state can distinguish persistent participation imbalance from price movement without broad support. The mechanism is valuable only if a fixed tuple remains profitable after costs, preserves material upside, reduces drawdown, improves Calmar, survives annual breadth and is stable at two frozen neighboring slow averages. Reduced participation alone cannot pass.",
  "opportunity_cost": "Test the strongest still-independent price-and-volume mechanism supported by a transaction-cost, multiple-testing and out-of-sample primary study before spending more capacity on DRA admission filters or new external sources.",
